.TH ANKER\-ACHIEVEMENTS 1 "2026-11-27" "anker-achievements" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
anker\-achievements \- make Steam achievements work in non-online AnkerGames titles
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B anker\-achievements
.B list
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
.P
.B anker\-achievements
.B fix
[\fIGAME\fR ...]
[\fB\-\-all\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry-run\fR]
[\fB\-\-refresh-schema\fR]
.P
.B anker\-achievements
.B auto
[\fB\-\-full\fR]
[\fB\-\-recent-hours\fR \fIHOURS\fR]
[\fB\-\-quiet\fR]
.P
.B anker\-achievements
.B restore
\fIGAME\fR ...
[\fB\-\-all\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry-run\fR]
.P
.B anker\-achievements
.B pool
[\fB\-\-download\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B anker\-achievements
converts the Steam emulator used by most AnkerGames releases from RUNE,
CODEX, EMPRESS or a similar crack to
.BR Goldberg
(gbe\_fork), then writes the game's real achievement definitions into
.IR steam_settings/achievements.json .
.P
Those cracks provide no achievement list. Games ask the emulator for the list,
receive nothing, and never call the Steamworks unlock API, so the Anker
Launcher's Achievements tab stays at zero. Goldberg reads a local schema, which
this tool obtains from the public Steam achievements page for the game's AppID.
.P
Online\-fix titles are never modified. Their emulator also carries the
multiplayer fix, and replacing it would break online play. The tool detects
.IR OnlineFix.ini
and skips the whole game.
.P
A conversion is recorded under
.IR ~/.local/share/anker\-achievements .
Original DLLs and old emulator state are copied to the backup directory before
anything is replaced, so
.B restore
can undo it.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS list
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the game table as JSON.
.SS fix
.TP
.BI GAME " ..."
Game ID, slug, or title substring. With no games, the default is every
installed title.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Explicitly select every installed title.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Print what would change without touching a file.
.TP
.B \-\-refresh-schema
Ignore the cached Steam schema and fetch it again.
.SS auto
.TP
.B \-\-full
Scan every played game instead of only games with a recently completed
install. This is what the daily timer uses.
.TP
.BI \-\-recent-hours " HOURS"
How far back to look for completed install events. Default: 6.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress lines for games that were skipped.
.SS restore
.TP
.BI GAME " ..."
Game ID, slug, or title substring.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Restore every game recorded in the state file.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Show what would be undone.
.SS pool
.TP
.B \-\-download
Download the latest gbe\_fork Windows release instead of reusing a Goldberg
DLL found in an installed game.
.SH BEHAVIOUR
.SS Conversion
For each eligible game the tool:
.IP \(bu 2
backs up \fIsteam_api64.dll\fR (or \fIsteam_api.dll\fR) outside the game folder;
.IP \(bu 2
copies the matching Goldberg binary in its place;
.IP \(bu 2
writes \fIsteam_appid.txt\fR and
.IR steam_settings/achievements.json ;
.IP \(bu 2
moves the old emulator's state out of
.IR "\fI<prefix>/drive_c/users/Public/Documents/Steam/RUNE/<appid>\fR"
and similar folders, so the launcher does not keep reading an empty
\fIachievements.ini\fR.
.P
Only the architecture the game actually uses is replaced. If a release ships
both API DLLs, the 64\-bit one wins.
.SS Automation
The companion systemd user units run the tool without user action:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBanker\-achievements.path\fR watches
\fI~/.config/net.ankergames.launcher\fR and runs
.B "auto"
after the launcher finishes an install or update;
.IP \(bu 2
\fBanker\-achievements-full.timer\fR runs
.B "auto \-\-full"
once a day and shortly after login as a safety net.
.P
Neither is a polling daemon. The path unit is event\-driven, and
.B auto
exits immediately when there is no new completed install to process. Games are
skipped while they are running, so a DLL is never replaced mid\-session.
.SS Limitations
Achievements already unlocked under the old emulator are not replayed. The
Steam backend decides when an achievement is awarded, and a save that predates
the conversion cannot re\-trigger events that already happened. New unlocks are
recorded from the first launch after conversion.
.SH EXAMPLES
See the current state of every installed game:
.IP
.EX
anker\-achievements list
.EE
.P
See what a full conversion would do:
.IP
.EX
anker\-achievements fix \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.P
Convert ROUTINE only:
.IP
.EX
anker\-achievements fix 3128
.EE
.P
Convert every non\-online title:
.IP
.EX
anker\-achievements fix \-\-all
.EE
.P
Undo the recorded changes for one game:
.IP
.EX
anker\-achievements restore 3128
.EE
.P
Run the same job the timer runs:
.IP
.EX
anker\-achievements auto \-\-full
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including a run where every game was skipped.
.TP
.B 1
Bad selection, no games matched, or a required download/extraction failed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/net.ankergames.launcher/library.json
Installed games and their Steam AppIDs.
.TP
.I ~/.config/net.ankergames.launcher/activity.json
Completed install events used by
.BR "auto" .
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/anker-achievements/
State, cached Steam schemas, the Goldberg DLL cache and backups.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/anker-achievements/backups/<game-id>/
Original DLLs and old emulator state.
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/anker-achievements.path
Event\-driven install hook.
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/anker-achievements-full.timer
Daily safety net.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR anker\-launcher (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR systemd.path (5),
.BR systemd.timer (5)
.SH AUTHOR
Written for local use.
